md-fast

parse.js is a port of marked 18.1.3 (https://github.com/markedjs/marked, tag v18.1.3,
commit ba50aa95636ac8f97f46446bbfeb04592ed22216), MIT licensed:

  Copyright (c) 2018+, MarkedJS. (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) 2011-2018, Christopher Jeffrey. (MIT License)

Its block and inline grammar (the regular expressions and the order in which marked tries them)
and the behaviour of its tokenizers are kept so that the output matches marked exactly; the lexer
loop, the inline text scanner, the renderer and the data flow are rewritten. marked's LICENSE,
which also carries the original Markdown notice (Copyright 2004, John Gruber), is kept unchanged
in LICENSE-marked.

No code of marked is executed or bundled at run time: marked is used only by the repository's
test tools, loaded from a separately downloaded copy.
That copy is the one the competition kit vendors (baselines/vendor/marked/marked.esm.js).

Where parse.js replaces one of marked's regular expressions or replace() calls by a scanner or an
index walk, the replaced expression is named in a comment next to it, so each can be checked
against marked's source.
